/* ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ARCHITECTURE OF GRACE — THE SITE BAR. ONE BAR, EVERY PAGE.

   Jimmy: "I WANT THE TOP BAR TO BE THE SAME ACROSS THE ENTIRE SITE. USE THE
   MAIN SITE AS THE ONE TO RUN OFF OF."

   So this IS the main site's bar — index.html's <header class="topbar">:
   the same mark, the same Quiet Space pill, the same Explore menu (the three
   doors, in the homepage's own numerals, names and bands), the same
   accessibility and theme buttons, the same EN|ES. Rebuilt as one file that
   any page can load in ONE line:

       <body>
       <script src="/aog-topbar.js"></script>

   ── HOW TO CHANGE IT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   AOG-BAR-ONEBAR-V1 (2026-09-25): the builder sources are not in this repo, so
   this file WAS hand-edited: the Economics row added, the Spanish and FACS
   lines matched to index.html, door three hidden as index.html hides it, and index.html now mounts THIS bar
   (its own <header class="topbar"> is hidden, not removed). If the builder
   comes back, fold these four changes into its sources first.
   Never hand-edit this file otherwise. It is generated by _work/topbar/build_topbar.py
   from aog-topbar-css.txt + aog-topbar-html.txt + aog-topbar-engine.js.
   Edit those and re-run the builder; then copy the result into BOTH
   aog-deploy/ and "AOG SITE/" (p_sitebar.py does that).

   ── FOUR THINGS THIS FILE KNOWS THAT COST A DAY TO LEARN ────────────────────

   ⚠⚠ 1. THE PAGE OWNS ITS OWN LANGUAGE, AND IT ALWAYS DID. Every standalone
   page carries `function paintLang()` INSIDE AN IIFE — unreachable from out
   here — and it translates far more than [data-en] spans (quiz items, hint
   decks, option labels). So the bar does NOT re-implement translation. It
   CLICKS the page's own #langBtn and lets that code do its job, and only
   falls back to swapping [data-en]/[data-es] itself on a page that has no
   language switch at all. Same for theme: it clicks #themeBtn. The page's
   switch is then hidden — NEVER TWO DOORS TO ONE PLACE.

   ⚠⚠ 2. THE PAGE'S OWN paintLang WILL REWRITE THIS BAR, and that is wanted:
   it walks EVERY [data-en] in the document, so the bar translates for free.
   It also does `el.textContent = v` unless the string contains "<b>", which
   means EVERY TRANSLATED SPAN IN THE MARKUP MUST BE A LEAF. Put a nested
   element inside a [data-en] span and the first language switch deletes it.

   ⚠⚠ 3. TWO STORAGE KEYS FOR ONE SETTING. index.html stores the theme at
   "aog.theme"; the 83 standalone pages store it at "aog.interior.ws.v1.theme"
   and read THAT in their own <head> before this file runs. Dark mode did not
   survive the walk between pages. The bar writes BOTH keys on every toggle
   and reconciles them at boot, which is what actually makes the setting
   follow a teacher from the home page into a worksheet and back.

   ⚠ 4. IT MOUNTS FIXED, NOT STICKY, WITH A SPACER. The bar lands on ~100
   pages with ~100 different layouts — centered columns, padded bodies, print
   sheets. position:sticky inherits the width and the padding of whatever box
   it lands in, so on a centered page it came out narrow and inset. Fixed +
   a measured spacer is the only shape that is identical everywhere.
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
